{"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/wt-v140.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/Client"],"title":"WebAuthn Client","generated":true,"anchor":"WebAuthn-Client"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/wt-v140.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn"},"metadata":{"externalID":"s:7YubiKit8WebAuthnO","modules":[{"name":"YubiKit"}],"roleHeading":"Enumeration","role":"symbol","title":"WebAuthn","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"WebAuthn"}],"symbolKind":"enum","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"WebAuthn"}]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/yubikit\/webauthn"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["iOS","iPadOS","Mac Catalyst"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"WebAuthn"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Contains the high-level passkey "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/wt-v140.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/Client"},{"type":"text","text":" and the request, response, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"data-model types defined by the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/www.w3.org\/TR\/webauthn-3\/"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"specification."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A passkey client and the W3C Web Authentication data model, mediated by a YubiKey."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WebAuthn"},{"type":"text","text":" namespace provides a high-level passkey client ("},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/wt-v140.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/Client"},{"type":"text","text":") that runs"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Web Authentication Level 3"}],"identifier":"https:\/\/www.w3.org\/TR\/webauthn-3\/","overridingTitle":"Web Authentication Level 3"},{"type":"text","text":" ceremonies against a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"YubiKey, plus the request and response types defined by the WebAuthn specification."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A WebAuthn ceremony involves three parties: the "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"authenticator"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (a YubiKey), the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"client"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (your app, via "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/wt-v140.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/Client"},{"type":"text","text":"), and the "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"relying party"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (your server, which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"verifies what the authenticator returns). The client is the communication path between"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"authenticator and relying party — and it verifies the relying party’s identity against"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the origin it’s bound to, so it can refuse to sign for a fraudulent site."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"There are two ceremonies. "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Registration"}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/wt-v140.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/Client\/makeCredential(_:authorization:)"},{"type":"text","text":") creates a new credential and supplies its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"public key to the relying party for account association. "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Authentication"}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/wt-v140.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/Client\/getAssertion(_:authorization:)"},{"type":"text","text":") proves to the relying party that the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"YubiKey is the one registered for the user. Both ceremonies follow the same mechanical"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"shape: the relying party supplies a challenge, the authenticator signs it together"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with the relying-party identifier, and the signature goes back to the relying party"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for verification."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The pieces fit together as: a connection carries CTAP2 traffic, a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/wt-v140.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/CTAP2\/Session"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sits on top, and "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/wt-v140.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/Client"},{"type":"text","text":" runs ceremonies on that session. Connections come in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"three flavours that all work for WebAuthn: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"YubiKit\/HIDFIDOConnection"},{"type":"text","text":" on macOS,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/wt-v140.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/NFCSmartCardConnection"},{"type":"text","text":" for tap-to-auth on iOS, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/wt-v140.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/USBSmartCardConnection"},{"type":"text","text":" on either platform. Pick the one that matches"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"your platform and form factor."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ macOS — USB HID FIDO","let connection = try await HIDFIDOConnection()","\/\/ iOS — tap-to-auth over NFC:","\/\/ let connection = try await NFCSmartCardConnection()","","let session = try await CTAP2.Session.makeSession(connection: connection)","let client = WebAuthn.Client(","    session: session,","    origin: try .init(\"https:\/\/example.com\"),","    isPublicSuffix: { publicSuffixList.contains($0) }",")","","\/\/ Register a new passkey","let registration = try await client.makeCredential(","    .init(","        challenge: challenge,","        rp: .init(id: \"example.com\", name: \"Example\"),","        user: .init(id: userId, name: \"alice@example.com\")","    ),","    authorization: .pin(\"1234\")",").value","","\/\/ Authenticate","let assertions = try await client.getAssertion(","    .init(challenge: challenge, rpId: \"example.com\"),","    authorization: .pin(\"1234\")",").value"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Most apps start with "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/wt-v140.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/Client"},{"type":"text","text":". For lower-level CTAP2 access — raw "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"makeCredential"},{"type":"text","text":" \/"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"getAssertion"},{"type":"text","text":", credential management, bio enrollment — use "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/wt-v140.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/CTAP2\/Session"},{"type":"text","text":" directly."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/wt-v140.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/Client","doc:\/\/wt-v140.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/Authorization","doc:\/\/wt-v140.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/Origin","doc:\/\/wt-v140.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/ClientError","doc:\/\/wt-v140.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/ClientData","doc:\/\/wt-v140.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/PublicSuffixChecker"],"title":"Client","anchor":"Client"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/wt-v140.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/Registration","doc:\/\/wt-v140.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/PublicKeyCredentialCreationOptions"],"title":"Registration (makeCredential)","anchor":"Registration-makeCredential"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/wt-v140.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/Authentication","doc:\/\/wt-v140.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/PublicKeyCredentialRequestOptions"],"title":"Authentication (getAssertion)","anchor":"Authentication-getAssertion"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/wt-v140.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/StatusStream","doc:\/\/wt-v140.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/Status"],"title":"Status Reporting","anchor":"Status-Reporting"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/wt-v140.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/RelyingParty","doc:\/\/wt-v140.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/User","doc:\/\/wt-v140.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/CredentialDescriptor","doc:\/\/wt-v140.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/Transport"],"title":"Relying Party and User Entities","anchor":"Relying-Party-and-User-Entities"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/wt-v140.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/ResidentKeyPreference","doc:\/\/wt-v140.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/UserVerificationPreference","doc:\/\/wt-v140.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/AttestationPreference"],"title":"Ceremony Preferences","anchor":"Ceremony-Preferences"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/wt-v140.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/AuthenticatorData","doc:\/\/wt-v140.YubiKit\/documen